# Lets the engine that currently owns an active RequestUserInput goal
# (rammp_ui_bridge_interfaces/action/RequestUserInput.action) change what's
# displayed to the user -- a new message/buttons, an updated candidate
# object list, and/or which object is currently highlighted as selected --
# without completing or restarting the goal. Typically called after a
# RequestUserInput feedback message reports an object tap, e.g. to change
# the panel's message to "<object> selected -- press Pick Up to continue"
# and highlight that object.
#
# Only valid while the calling engine's RequestUserInput goal is still
# active; refused (accepted=false) if there is no active goal, or if
# `token` doesn't match the one currently granted (see
# ~/ui_control/acquire_control, same resource RequestUserInput's own
# token is checked against).
#
# `update_panel`/`panel_json`/`update_objects`/`objects`/`update_selected`/
# `selected_instance_id` were previously three independent (bool flag,
# value) pairs. They are now folded into one `request_json` JSON string
# (same shape as RequestUserInput.Goal's `request_json`, see
# rammp-UI-bridge docs/INTERACTION_PANEL_SCHEMA.md): presence of a key
# means "replace this aspect", and a key's absence means "leave it
# unchanged" -- there is no longer a separate bool alongside each value.

uint8[16] token
string request_json
# JSON object, every key optional -- only present keys are updated, an
# absent key leaves that aspect of the panel/candidate list/selection
# unchanged:
#   {
#     "panel_json": str,          # replaces the current panel entirely, iff present
#     "objects": [                # replaces the current candidate list entirely, iff present
#       {"instance_id": str, "perception_class": str, "box": [x_min, y_min, x_max, y_max]}
#     ],
#     "selected_instance_id": str  # highlight this instance_id ("" clears any highlight),
#                                 # iff present
#   }
---
bool accepted
string message
